            {
              "id": "art-body",
              "type": "column",
              "props": {
                "span": 9
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When it comes to running a profitable trucking operation, every decision matters, but few choices have as much long-term impact as the parts for semi-trucks you install.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At first glance, cheaper parts may seem like a smart way to cut costs. But over time, those short-term savings often lead to higher repair bills, more downtime, and reduced reliability.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At Sun State International, we work closely with owner-operators and fleet managers across Florida who've learned this lesson the hard way. The reality is simple: not all truck parts are created equal, and choosing the wrong ones can quietly drain your operation's profitability.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "We break down the real costs behind cheap components, explain OEM vs aftermarket truck parts, and help you make smarter decisions that protect your truck, your schedule, and your bottom line.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-why-parts-matter",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Parts for Semi-Trucks Matter More Than You Think",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "why-parts-matter"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-parts-matter-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A semi truck isn't just a vehicle; it's a revenue-producing asset. Every hour it's off the road costs money. That's why truck parts reliability plays such a critical role in overall performance and operating costs. Low-quality or mismatched parts can lead to:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-why-parts-matter-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Premature failures"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Repeat repairs"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Additional damage to surrounding components"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Increased labor costs"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Unplanned downtime"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-parts-matter-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "While cutting corners on parts may reduce the upfront invoice, it often increases the total cost of ownership over the life of the truck.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-real-cost",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The Real Cost of Cheap Semi Truck Replacement Parts",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "real-cost"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-real-cost-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Cheap parts tend to fail faster. That means you're not just paying for the part; you're paying for labor, lost driving time, and sometimes towing or roadside repairs. Unplanned downtime can cost fleets hundreds of dollars per hour per truck when you factor in labor, missed loads, and cascading delays. Even for owner-operators, a single breakdown can disrupt an entire week's schedule. This is where the hidden costs add up:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-real-cost-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "A lower-priced part that lasts half as long"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Additional labor to install replacements"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Increased stress on other systems"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Reduced confidence in your equipment"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-real-cost-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Over time, these issues outweigh the initial savings and drive up long-term operating costs.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-1",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/avoid-cheap-parts-how-to-find-reliable-parts-for-semi-trucks/1.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 853,
                      "alt": "Sun State International parts team pulling and verifying components at the parts counter"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-oem-vs-aftermarket",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "OEM vs Aftermarket Truck Parts: What's the Difference?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "oem-vs-aftermarket"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-oem-vs-aftermarket-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Understanding OEM vs aftermarket truck parts is key to making informed decisions.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-oem-vs-aftermarket-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "compare",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "OEM (Original Equipment Manufacturer) Parts",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "Proven fit and compatibility"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Consistent performance"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Often longer service life"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Better support for warranties"
                          }
                        ],
                        "intro": "OEM parts are built to the exact specifications of your truck's original components. They're designed to fit precisely, perform consistently, and meet manufacturer standards."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Aftermarket Truck Parts",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "The manufacturer is reputable"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "The application is non-critical"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "The part meets or exceeds OEM specifications"
                          }
                        ],
                        "intro": "Aftermarket parts are produced by third-party manufacturers. Some offer excellent value and performance, while others prioritize price over durability. Aftermarket parts can be a good option when:"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-oem-vs-aftermarket-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The key is knowing which aftermarket parts are reliable, and which ones to avoid.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-long-term-roi",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "How Quality Truck Parts Protect Long-Term ROI",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "long-term-roi"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-long-term-roi-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Choosing quality truck parts isn't about buying the most expensive option; it's about buying the right option. Reliable parts reduce repeat repairs, protect major systems, and help maintain consistent performance. High-quality heavy-duty truck parts contribute to:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-long-term-roi-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Fewer breakdowns"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "More predictable maintenance schedules"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Improved driver confidence"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Higher resale value"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-long-term-roi-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "In other words, quality parts help your truck stay productive longer, which is exactly what owner-operators and fleets need to stay competitive.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "co-long-term-roi-4-row",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 0
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "co-long-term-roi-4",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "styles": {
